        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Psychopathology studies psychological disorders: how they are described, how they develop, how they affect people, and how they may be treated. The subject asks difficult questions. When does an understandable human reaction become a disorder? Why did people once blame spirits for unusual behavior? What can we learn from biological explanations without ignoring learning, emotions, or society?"
