        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "A dysfunction involves a problem in cognitive, emotional or behavioral functioning. Cognition concerns processes such as attention, perception and interpretation. Emotion concerns responses such as fear or sadness. Behavior concerns actions, including avoidance. A strong reaction does not automatically indicate dysfunction: fear may be useful when there is a genuine threat. The question is whether a process is operating in a way that is seriously mismatched to the situation or difficult to regulate."
