        "text": "Distress means significant suffering. Impairment means difficulty participating in important parts of life, such as studying, working, forming relationships or caring for oneself. They are related but not identical. A person may experience intense grief after a death without having a disorder; distress can be an understandable response to loss. Conversely, during a manic episode a person may report feeling unusually well while their judgment, finances or relationships are severely affected. The absence of acknowledged distress therefore does not settle the question."
